Fix out-of-bounds read in the hmtx trailing-advance-width optimization.

The loop counts down a size_t while comparing against the last glyph's
advance width. When every advance width matches it, the index decrements
below zero, wraps to SIZE_MAX and indexes the vector out of bounds. On
libc++ the hardened operator[] traps this, so every addfeatures/makeotf
run crashes with SIGTRAP; on libstdc++ it is silently undefined behavior.

Rewrite the scan to keep the index strictly positive and track the number
of leading entries to retain instead.

Not yet submitted upstream; the bug is present in afdko main as of 5.0.1.

diff --git i/c/addfeatures/hotconv/hmtx.cpp w/c/addfeatures/hotconv/hmtx.cpp
index 9336c986..f11cafd9 100644
--- i/c/addfeatures/hotconv/hmtx.cpp
+++ w/c/addfeatures/hotconv/hmtx.cpp
@@ -51,13 +51,14 @@ int hmtxFill(hotCtx g) {

     /* Optimize metrics */
     FWord width = hmtx.advanceWidth.back();
-    size_t i;
-    for (i = hmtx.advanceWidth.size() - 2; i >= 0; i--) {
-        if (hmtx.advanceWidth[i] != width)
+    size_t keep = 1;
+    for (size_t i = hmtx.advanceWidth.size(); i > 1; i--) {
+        if (hmtx.advanceWidth[i - 2] != width) {
+            keep = i;
             break;
+        }
     }
-    if (i + 2 != hmtx.advanceWidth.size())
-        hmtx.advanceWidth.resize(i+2);
+    hmtx.advanceWidth.resize(keep);

     return hmtx.Fill();
 }
